{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSd7yKeWFZCQRBa1K4u8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\nBased on my analysis, here's my proposed design:\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### 1. **Order.kt** - Add status field\n- Add an `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values\n- Add a `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class\n- Default new orders to `ACTIVE`\n\n### 2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add methods for status management and shipment lookup\n- Add `findByOrderIdForCancellation(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to get shipments by orderId\n  - Actually, this belongs in ShipmentRepository, not OrderRepository\n- Add update capability (or rely on save for re-storing order)\n\n### 3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add shipment lookup by orderId\n- Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method\n- Update shipment status through save (existing pattern)\n\n### 4. **OrderController.kt** - Add cancel endpoint\n- Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` that:\n  - Returns 404 if order not found\n  - If order is already CANCELLED, returns 200 with the order (idempotent)\n  - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, returns 409 with no changes\n  - Otherwise, moves order to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, persists all changes, returns the order\n\n### 5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Validate against cancelled orders\n- Inject OrderRepository \n- When creating shipment, check if order exists and is CANCELLED\n- If yes, throw ConflictException with appropriate error code\n\n### 6. **ApiError.kt** - Add error code\n- Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum (for shipment creation on cancelled orders)\n\n### 7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for cancel functionality\n- Test cancelling an ACTIVE order\n- Test cancelling an already CANCELLED order (idempotent)\n- Test cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment\n- Test cancel on non-existent order (404)\n- Test that cancellation cancels CREATED shipments\n\n### 8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Verify existing tests and add new ones\n- Verify existing tests still pass\n- Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order returns 409\n\n## Alternatives Rejected\n\n**Alternative 1: Store order status in a separate map**\n- Rejected because it complicates the code and violates the single-source-of-truth pattern. The Order entity should own its own state.\n\n**Alternative 2: Use @Transactional**\n- Rejected because we're using in-memory storage, not a database. The existing codebase doesn't use @Transactional and Spring Data JPA is not in the dependencies.\n\n**Alternative 3: Create a new OrderService layer**\n- Rejected because the existing OrderController directly uses the repository. Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring outside the ticket scope.\n\n## Data and Error Flow\n\n### Cancel Active Order → Cancelled\n1. **Input**: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n2. **Read**: OrderRepository finds order by orderId\n3. **Check**: If order doesn't exist → throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND) → 404\n4. **Check**: If order.status == CANCELLED → return 200 with order (idempotent)\n5. **Check**: Get all shipments for this order from ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId)\n6. **Check**: If any shipment.status == CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED) → 409, no changes\n7. **Update**: Set order.status = CANCELLED, save to repository\n8. **Update**: For each shipment with status CREATED, set status = CANCELLED, save to repository\n9. **Return**: 200 OK with updated order\n\n### Create Shipment Against Cancelled Order\n1. **Input**: `POST /shipments` with orderId\n2. **Read**: OrderRepository finds order by orderId\n3. **Check**: If order.status == CANCELLED → throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) → 409\n4. **Check**: If order not found, continue (existing behavior per requirement)\n5. **Create**: Create shipment with status CREATED\n\n## Test Strategy\n\n**OrderControllerTest additions:**\n- Test 1: Cancel an ACTIVE order succeeds and returns the order with CANCELLED status\n- Test 2: Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n- Test 3: Cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with error code\n- Test 4: Cancelling non-existent order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n- Test 5: Cancelling an order cancels all its CREATED shipments\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest additions:**\n- Test 1: Creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n1. `Order.kt` - Add status field and enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` - Add cancel endpoint\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` - Add method to find shipments by orderId (no, this goes in ShipmentRepository)\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Add findByOrderId method\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add order validation\n6. `ApiError.kt` - Add error codes\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - Add cancel tests\n8. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add validation test (if needed)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:\n\n### 1. Update Order.kt to add status field"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2143,"cache_read_input_tokens":23282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2143},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b16af89b-522d-4463-b7cb-606767672c25","uuid":"d3533d50-8545-4b70-ad0b-35fe95aec936","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:44:14.854Z","request_id":"req_011CfSd7xwapAWYGgJHUbvpw"}
